---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Pools in MBR City"
  description="Pool access across MBR City's communities — building pools versus District One's Crystal Lagoon, and what's actually available where."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Pools</p>
    <h1>Building pools, and the one district-scale exception</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Pool access in MBR City is mostly a per-building amenity, the same as
      anywhere else in Dubai — District One's Crystal Lagoon is the one
      community-scale exception, and it's a different kind of amenity, not
      a bigger version of a building pool.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Building pools</h2>
    <p>
      A shared residents' pool is standard across apartment buildings in
      Riviera and Sobha Hartland, and common in Meydan's mid-rise
      buildings too — see <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc/pools/">Riviera's
      own pools page</a> for what's typical there specifically. Villa
      communities like District One more often have private pools per unit
      instead of a shared building pool.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>District One's Crystal Lagoon</h2>
    <p>
      A large artificial lagoon, not a conventional "pool" — see the
      <a href="/water/">water page</a> for the honest version of what it
      offers and who actually has access to it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

